<section class="hero">
  <h1 class="hero__title">
    Fix your Rails app
    <span class="pen-mark">on the page<svg viewBox="0 0 240 14" preserveAspectRatio="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 9 C 45 3, 92 12, 138 7 S 214 4, 237 8"/></svg></span>.
  </h1>
  <p class="hero__lead">Edit the text where you see it. Tensaku writes it back to the source.</p>
  <div class="hero__actions">
    <a class="button button--ink" href="#try">Try it on this page</a>
    <a class="button" href="/installation">Install it</a>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="try" id="try">
  <ol class="try__steps">
    <li><strong>Alt-click</strong> the big heading, change a word and press Enter.</li>
    <li>Press <kbd>Alt</kbd> <kbd>Shift</kbd> <kbd>T</kbd>, click a card below and choose <strong>Add note</strong>.</li>
    <li>Press <strong>Resolve as the agent</strong> and watch the pin turn green.</li>
  </ol>
  <p class="try__touch">On a touch screen, tap 添 in the corner, then Edit.</p>
</section>

<%= render "demo/window" %>

<section class="features">
  <article>
    <h3><span class="ink-red">Edit</span> text in place</h3>
    <p>The editor shows the source. Ruby stays a locked chip, so you only change the words around it.</p>
  </article>
  <article>
    <h3><span class="ink-blue">Notes</span> for your agent</h3>
    <p>Point at anything and say what should change. Your agent gets the note with the file and line.</p>
  </article>
  <article>
    <h3><span class="ink-green">Production</span> stays the same</h3>
    <p>Tensaku only loads in development, and every write touches only the bytes you edited.</p>
  </article>
</section>

<section class="install">
  <h2>Two commands</h2>
  <pre class="install__code"><code>bundle add tensaku --group development
bin/rails generate tensaku:install</code></pre>
  <p>Ruby 4.0 and Rails 8.1 or later. <a href="/introduction">Read the docs</a></p>
</section>
